{
  "comment": "Hand-written golden of block behaviour values, read by hand from upstream 4.8 (9e40a757) src/main/java/gloamingforest/init/GloamingBlocks.java, the block classes' getExplosionResistance / getDestroyProgress overrides and Minecraft 1.21.1's Blocks.java (for ofFullCopy(Blocks.X) / copyAndScaleProperties(Blocks.X, k)); independent of the generator. hardness: Java destroyTime or 'unbreakable' (-1); resistance: Java explosionResistance (BlockBehaviour.Properties.of() defaults both to 0; strength(f) sets both, destroyTime / explosionResistance only their own) or 'indestructible' (3600000 and above, Float.MAX_VALUE); sound: the Java SoundType; mapColor: the Java MapColor (null: none). cases: the value in a given state where a class override makes it state-dependent (other states keep the block's values). tools: the tools that mine it faster, from upstream's tag JSONs (pickaxe / axe / shovel / hoe: #minecraft:mineable/<kind>; sword: #minecraft:sword_efficient; leaves: #minecraft:leaves (the Bedrock tag minecraft:leaves); shears: #minecraft:leaves or #minecraft:wool (minecraft:is_shears_item_destructible); with the vanilla 1.21.1 tags these include, e.g. #minecraft:planks in mineable/axe); tier: #minecraft:needs_<tier>_tool of a block a tool mines; requiresTool: requiresCorrectToolForDrops() in GloamingBlocks.java (also through ofFullCopy). Units: Java's; the import writes explosion_resistance = resistance x 5 (Bedrock stores a fifth of the JSON value, measured on 1.26.51). tools/import/src/Checks.cs (CheckBehaviour) compares the generated BP block files and RP block sounds with it on every run.",
